    "description": "North Carolina Solar is a portfolio of utility-scale solar projects in North Carolina. The customer base is anchored by contracted power sales, with public sources referencing busbar PPAs with Duke Energy Progress. The portfolio is asset-heavy because value is derived from operating generation assets rather than development services alone. John Laing's portfolio page describes five operating projects totaling 334 MW, with commercial operation dates spanning late 2018 to early 2019. The reviewed materials did not disclose current revenue, project-level leverage, or the economic split within John Laing Investments Limited. The asset is associated in the master workbook with John Laing Investments Limited, the holding structure backed by Equitix and KKR.",
